cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use polypack in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "polypack: certified search and verification for packings of regular polygons in regular polygons"
authors:
  - family-names: Papowitz
    given-names: Aristotle
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-17
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/AriPapowitz/polygon-packing-records"
keywords:
  - packing problems
  - computational geometry
  - global optimization
  - certified computation
  - experimental mathematics
  - JAX
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for finding and certifying record packings of unit regular
  polygons in minimal regular polygon containers: a batched float32/float64
  GPU search engine, an independent exact separating-axis certifier with
  rigorous dilation bounds, image-to-coordinates reconstruction of published
  packings, structured basin-hopping and drop-one record mechanisms,
  high-precision contact solving with residual-validated PSLQ, and
  benchmark scrape/archive tooling. The toolkit behind a 2026 record
  campaign on Erich Friedman's Packing Center (52 credited improvements).
